<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Code-to-model traceability: 75/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The decoding rule, the coordinate convention (+y anterior, wild-type head->trunk angle 3pi/2) and the cartoon convention are documented where they are implemented, and region_outline() names the figure it reproduces. The radii-count rule was established by checking the database rather than quoted from a numbered equation, because the papers describe the formalism in prose." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 7.5e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Model fidelity to source: 85/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Region shape parameters are interpreted with the formalism's own rule (0 links -> 4 radii right/anterior/left/posterior; 1 link -> +90/+180/+270 deg from the edge; k >= 2 links -> one radius per bisector of consecutive edges), region centres are placed from the RegionsLink Dist/Ang labels and borders at Ratio*Dist, and the rule is checked at load time against all 1181 regions in the database. The only element not taken from the source is how consecutive control radii are joined: a superellipse arc (n = 2.2 free, n = 7 at a border) chosen to reproduce Planform's Fig. 1D; the paper does not publish Planform's interpolant." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-model-fidelity-5> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.5e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Morphometric validation: 45/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script computes silhouette morphometrics (AP length, ML width, aspect, area, region and organ counts, length relative to wild type) for every morphology and can write them as CSV, and the measurements sidecar checks the decoded wild type against the radii encoded in the database (560 x 120 units). Nothing is yet compared with measurements of real animals or with values reported in the literature; the reference is the formalism, not a specimen." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-measurement-distinct-body-silhouettes>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-measurement-distinct-encodings-regions-links-organs>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-measurement-iou-wild-type-vs-double-head-24>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-measurement-iou-wild-type-vs-headless-20>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-measurement-morphologies-rendered>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-measurement-wild-type-ap-ml-aspect>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-measurement-wild-type-silhouette-ap-length>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-measurement-wild-type-silhouette-ml-width>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-morphometric-validation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-morphometric-validation-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 4.5e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — MorphoEval overall 66.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Rewritten. The region graph of every PlanformDB morphology is now decoded exactly (polar radii per region, centres and borders from the RegionsLink labels, organs from the organ table) and drawn in Planform's own cartoon convention; wild type, double head, headless, cyclops and the other canonical phenotypes are visually distinct and recognisable as Planform drawings. Remaining gap: the formalism stores three radii per head, so species features such as auricles or a triangular head are not in the data and the renders still read as cartoons, not specimens. Overall 66.5/100 (faithfulness 66.1, reproducibility 67.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 161f269; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 85, Morphological realism / specimen match 60, Parameter expressivity 75, Morphometric validation 45, Source and data traceability 70, Code-to-model traceability 75, Reproducibility package 60. Output judged: planform_morphology_gallery.png: rendered output of 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py at 161f269, image/png, 443915 B, 1920×2160 px, artifact_sha256 77a7dfa087bf89441dc35c64bc0c96bccfdc15d44a3d600df766fb723a87ace5 (sha256 77a7dfa087bf89441dc35c64bc0c96bccfdc15d44a3d600df766fb723a87ace5)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add per-species outline templates (auricles, head shape) layered on the decoded regions, clearly marked as not from the database.",
        "remediation needed: Compare the decoded aspect ratio and organ positions with measurements on photographed S. mediterranea / D. japonica.",
        "remediation needed: Pin dependency versions for the Python 3.14 environment used here.",
        "remediation needed: Record the sha256 and version of the PlanformDB file used, and its download location." ;
    pk1:hasScore 6.65e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Parameter expressivity: 75/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Every encoded quantity now has a visible effect: each radius moves one control point of its region, each link moves a region centre and a border, each organ vector/rotation places one organ. All morphologies in a frame share one scale (frame_bounds), so the size and proportion differences between phenotypes are preserved. The final morphospace grid of the timeline fits each morphology to its cell, which deliberately trades scale for legibility." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-parameter-expressivity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-parameter-expressivity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 7.5e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Reproducibility package: 60/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Deterministic (no random state), invocation documented in the docstring and README, outputs reproduced identically on re-run, and morphologies with no encoded regions are skipped with a message rather than failing. Dependencies (numpy, scipy, matplotlib, Pillow) are in requirements.txt with lower bounds only, and the run depends on an unversioned external database." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-repro-package-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 6e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-source-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Source and data traceability: 70/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Both source papers are cited with DOIs in the module docstring, the database version is named and the schema tables used are listed. The database itself is still an external file located through PLANFORM_DB_PATH; no hash or download URL is recorded, so the exact input cannot be verified from the repository alone." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-source-traceability-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 7e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Morphological realism / specimen match: 60/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Side by side with Planform's Fig. 1D (Biology Open) the wild type now has the same structure: a straight-sided body with flat head/trunk and trunk/tail borders, rounded caps, red head fading to pink, blue tail, oval eyes with pupils, green brain lobes and nerve cords, a tube pharynx. Double head (#24), headless (#20), cyclops, side heads and polarity-reversed morphologies are told apart at a glance; 167 distinct body silhouettes among 369 morphologies, the rest (115 of them wild-type bodied) differing only in organs, which is how the database encodes them. Against a photographed S. mediterranea the match is weaker: no auricles, no triangular head, no pigmentation; these are not encoded in the database." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-specimen-match-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 6e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

